            "rawHtml": "<h3>02 -- THREE APPROACHES</h3><p class=\"lead-statement\">Three Ways to Segment East-West Traffic Without strong segmentation, any port or server can reach any other -- so a single breach can spread freely. These</p><div class=\"info-card mt-3\"><p>three approaches can be combined for increasingly granular control. Environment Segmentation Separates entire environments -- e.g. development from production. The first, foundational stage of any segmentation strategy. Application Segmentation &quot;Ringfences&quot; high-value applications, isolating each critical app from the rest of the network -- down to the process level. Tier Segmentation The tightest form: policy within an application itself, controlling traffic between web, application, and database tiers. NETWORK SEGMENTATION &amp; MICROSEGMENTATION 7</p></div>",
