            "lead": "03 -- VLANS Example Scenario: Reconfiguring a VLAN Segment A network team needs to add a new segment for a business unit's servers. Here's what that typically looks like with",
            "isTitleSlide": false,
            "isSectionDivider": false,
            "rawHtml": "<h3>03 -- VLANS: Example Scenario: Reconfiguring a VLAN Segment</h3><p class=\"lead-statement\">Example Scenario: Reconfiguring a VLAN Segment A network team needs to add a new segment for a business unit&#x27;s servers. Here&#x27;s what that typically looks like with</p><div class=\"info-card mt-3\"><p>VLANs. 1 Map dependencies Engineers manually document every server and dependency in the target segment 2 Design the config New switch-level configuration is drafted for each affected switch 3 Schedule a window Because traffic may be interrupted, the change needs a maintenance window 4 Roll out across sites Multiple physical locations mean the same change repeated many times over Result: a process that can take many days and cost a disproportionate amount of time and money -- while traffic sits interrupted or slowed. NETWORK SEGMENTATION &amp; MICROSEGMENTATION 11</p></div>",
