            "subtitle": "Approach Two: Application Segmentation (Layer 4)",
            "lead": "04 -- LAYER 4 CONTROLS The Limits of Layer 4 Controls Layer 4 controls are essential, but attackers have shown they can work around IP- and port-based rules -- and Layer",
            "isTitleSlide": false,
            "isSectionDivider": false,
            "rawHtml": "<h3>04 -- LAYER 4 CONTROLS</h3><p class=\"lead-statement\">The Limits of Layer 4 Controls Layer 4 controls are essential, but attackers have shown they can work around IP- and port-based rules -- and Layer</p><div class=\"info-card mt-3\"><p>4 does nothing to stop movement once inside a tier. IP spoofing Attackers can forge source IP addresses to slip past rules written only against IP ranges. Port piggybacking Malicious traffic hides inside open, legitimate application ports -- the port is allowed, so Layer 4 waves it through. No intra-tier control Layer 4 protection doesn&#x27;t limit lateral movement within an application or a single tier once an attacker is inside it. The key insight: a Layer 4 port is either open or closed. It can&#x27;t tell the difference between the right process using that port and the wrong one impersonating it. NETWORK SEGMENTATION &amp; MICROSEGMENTATION 14</p></div>",
            "cleanText": "04 -- LAYER 4 CONTROLS The Limits of Layer 4 Controls Layer 4 controls are essential, but attackers have shown they can work around IP- and port-based rules -- and Layer 4 does nothing to stop movement once inside a tier. IP spoofing Attackers can forge source IP addresses to slip past rules written only against IP ranges. Port piggybacking Malicious traffic hides inside open, legitimate application ports -- the port is allowed, so Layer 4 waves it through. No intra-tier control Layer 4 protection doesn't limit lateral movement within an application or a single tier once an attacker is inside it. The key insight: a Layer 4 port is either open or closed. It can't tell the difference between the right process using that port and the wrong one impersonating it. NETWORK SEGMENTATION & MICROSEGMENTATION 14",
