            "subtitle": "Approach Two: Application Segmentation (Layer 4)",
            "lead": "04 -- LAYER 4 CONTROLS Compliant Isn't the Same as Secure Layer 4 segmentation has historically been accepted for regulatory scope reduction -- keeping a CDE separate for",
            "isTitleSlide": false,
            "isSectionDivider": false,
            "rawHtml": "<h3>04 -- LAYER 4 CONTROLS</h3><p class=\"lead-statement\">Compliant Isn&#x27;t the Same as Secure Layer 4 segmentation has historically been accepted for regulatory scope reduction -- keeping a CDE separate for</p><div class=\"info-card mt-3\"><p>PCI-DSS, or isolating PHI for HIPAA. But compliance and security are not the same test. 43% of companies are &quot;fully compliant&quot; with PCI-DSS, per Verizon&#x27;s 2022 Payment Security Report 100% compliance still doesn&#x27;t mean 100% security -- attackers can ride an open Layer 4 port straight to Layer 7 and take what they want Source: Verizon 2022 Payment Security Report -- cited in Akamai&#x27;s Network Segmentation and Microsegmentation white paper. Layer 4 controls may satisfy an auditor -- they don&#x27;t reduce the attack surface enough to make a meaningful security difference on their own. NETWORK SEGMENTATION &amp; MICROSEGMENTATION 15</p></div>",
            "cleanText": "04 -- LAYER 4 CONTROLS Compliant Isn't the Same as Secure Layer 4 segmentation has historically been accepted for regulatory scope reduction -- keeping a CDE separate for PCI-DSS, or isolating PHI for HIPAA. But compliance and security are not the same test. 43% of companies are \"fully compliant\" with PCI-DSS, per Verizon's 2022 Payment Security Report 100% compliance still doesn't mean 100% security -- attackers can ride an open Layer 4 port straight to Layer 7 and take what they want Source: Verizon 2022 Payment Security Report -- cited in Akamai's Network Segmentation and Microsegmentation white paper. Layer 4 controls may satisfy an auditor -- they don't reduce the attack surface enough to make a meaningful security difference on their own. NETWORK SEGMENTATION & MICROSEGMENTATION 15",
