            "lead": "05 -- LAYER 7 MICROSEGMENTATION Example Scenario: Process-Level Allowlisting An app server is allowed to reach the database only via its known, signed payment process -- on the exact expected port.",
            "isTitleSlide": false,
            "isSectionDivider": false,
            "rawHtml": "<h3>05 -- LAYER 7 MICROSEGMENTATION</h3><p class=\"lead-statement\">Example Scenario: Process-Level Allowlisting An app server is allowed to reach the database only via its known, signed payment process -- on the exact expected port.</p><div class=\"info-card mt-3\"><p>Everything else is blocked by default, automatically. App Server payment-svc.exe hash: a1f9...c02e (verified) attempted-shell.exe hash: 7bd2...91aa (unknown) Database Only payment-svc.exe with a verified hash is allowlisted on port 5432. allowed blocked -- unrecognized process Even a process that mirrors the right pathway or port is stopped -- because the policy checks the process identity itself, not just the network path. NETWORK SEGMENTATION &amp; MICROSEGMENTATION 18</p></div>",
