            "subtitle": "Approach Three: Microsegmentation to Layer 7 & Ransomware Defense",
            "lead": "CONCLUSION Future-Proof the Business With Microsegmentation",
            "isTitleSlide": false,
            "isSectionDivider": false,
            "rawHtml": "<div class=\"intro-author-card\"><div class=\"institution-badge\"><span>West Visayas State University • CICT Main Campus, Iloilo City</span></div><h2>Thank You!</h2><p class=\"intro-tagline\">CIT 220 Information Assurance and Security 2 • Unit 02.2 Complete</p><p class=\"mt-4 text-xs text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400\">Curriculum instruction by Prof. Chin Ann Feliprada • WVSU CICT</p></div>",
            "cleanText": "CONCLUSION Future-Proof the Business With Microsegmentation Start with environment segmentation It's the crucial first stage -- separate dev, prod, and other environments before going more granular. Layer the three approaches Environment, application, and tier segmentation combine to build increasingly granular policy for critical apps. Push to Layer 7 where it matters Process- and flow-level control catches what IP- and port-based rules alone will miss. Demand real visibility A segmentation solution that can't show you what's happening, in real time, isn't enough. A good microsegmentation solution won't ask you to choose between security and agility. Source material: \"Network Segmentation and Microsegmentation in Modern Enterprise Environments,\" Akamai White Paper, published 05/23. akamai.com/guardicore NETWORK SEGMENTATION & MICROSEGMENTATION 25",
